.TH "initSecurityKeys" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
initSecurityKeys \- initialize the key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.initSecurityKeys()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to initialize the key.
After the initialization is successful, the "MK" key and "DEK" key will be
generated and stored in the directory \f[C]<catalog_dbpath>/security/MK\f[] and
\f[C]<catalog_dbpath>/security/DEK\f[], the file description can refer to key
file.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[]
.PP
Currently only supports executing this function through local connection.
.RE
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
